{{Heroic_Card_Infobox|Cost=4|AbilityCost=2|Rarity=Legendary|Type=Troop|Arena=Rascal's Hideout|ReleaseDate=March 2,2026}}
{{Quote|With every pinecone a target and every branch a new vantage point, Hero Magic Archer was favored to be Forest Gang's first Hero. Being Boss Bandit's right hand comes with a few perks!}}
The Heroic Magic Archer is a {{Rarity|Common}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked with 200 {{Icon|I=Hero Shard}}. It spawns an area damage, air-targeting, long-ranged, ground [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] with moderate hitpoints and moderate damage. The Magic Archer launches an attack that travels up to its maximum range, while piercing through enemies. He takes the appearance of a man with gray hair with white stripes, glowing turquoise eyes, bushy black eyebrows, and a French-fork beard, wears a dark green tunic, a team-colored cape, a brown belt with a triangular copper rune and fingerless gloves, and dark brown pants and boots, and wields a glowing team-colored bow. A Heroic Magic Archer card costs 3 {{Icon|I=Elixir}} to deploy.

== Ability: Triple Threat ==
{{Quote|Summons a decoy while darting back and fires a triple shot on his next attack.}}{{Hero Ability|2=Triple Threat}}
The Hero Knight has a special ability accessible from whatever side of the screen was put in, just above the player's [[Cards|card]] slots in [[Basics of Battle|battle]]. When activated, the Magic Archer will teleport back, while leaving a decoy in his place. The next attack now shots 3 arrows that travel longer, but with less damage. The Triple Threat ability costs 2 [[Elixir]] to activate.

== Strategy ==
*The ability can be used to avoid damage from spells like [[Fireball]] or units like [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], thanks to the pull back and decoy.
*The arrows can deal good chip damage to towers

